#!/bin/sh
# tailscale (daemon+forwards+publish) moved to the router container - see
# docs/router.md and .claude/backlog/functional-router-plan.md. This script
# used to restart code-docker's own tailscale-forward program via the local
# supervisorctl socket; that program doesn't exist here anymore, so this now
# just explains the new procedure instead of silently doing nothing.
cat <<'EOF'
forward-reload: tailscale (forwards/publish) now runs on the router
container, not code-docker - this command can't reach it from here anymore.

Edit the config on the host at ${ROUTER_VOLUME:-./data/router}/tailscale/config.yaml,
then reload from the host (not from inside code-docker) with:

  docker compose exec code-docker-router supervisorctl restart tailscale-forward tailscale-publish

See docs/router.md for details.
EOF
exit 1
